1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,312
Three friends.

2
00:00:01,312 --> 00:00:03,117
Three totally different tastes.

3
00:00:03,117 --> 00:00:04,124
One trip.

4
00:00:04,124 --> 00:00:05,618
So who gets their way?

5
00:00:05,618 --> 00:00:07,990
With TasteMatch Trips, everyone does.

6
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:10,747
Group trips usually get planned for the

7
00:00:10,747 --> 00:00:12,867
majority, or for the loudest friend.

8
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:15,263
And someone always ends up dragged along.

9
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:16,842
This is the live app.

10
00:00:16,842 --> 00:00:18,420
Each friend adds a nickname

11
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,999
and a couple of favourites.

12
00:00:19,999 --> 00:00:22,950
Aziz loves Interstellar and Patagonia.

13
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,867
Malika, Daft Punk and Wes Anderson.

14
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:29,040
Rustam, Anthony Bourdain and Chef's Table.

15
00:00:29,817 --> 00:00:31,792
One click, and the agent goes

16
00:00:31,792 --> 00:00:33,632
to work on Qloo's live API.

17
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:35,588
Thirteen calls, about a second.

18
00:00:36,183 --> 00:00:38,193
Sayulita, Mexico.

19
00:00:38,193 --> 00:00:39,987
Group fit: eighty.

20
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:42,664
Malika is at ninety percent, and even

21
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:46,352
the least-matched friend, Rustam, gets seventy-six.

22
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:49,374
Every city is ranked by fairness: forty

23
00:00:49,374 --> 00:00:52,116
percent average, forty percent the least happy

24
00:00:52,116 --> 00:00:54,500
traveler, twenty percent group affinity.

25
00:00:55,217 --> 00:00:58,373
Then a two-day plan built from Qloo's local places.

26
00:00:58,373 --> 00:01:00,874
It's shared round-robin, so everyone gets two

27
00:01:00,874 --> 00:01:02,763
picks of their own, and every stop

28
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:04,542
shows the Qloo signal behind it.

29
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,398
All six stops on one map, plus a

30
00:01:07,398 --> 00:01:10,084
trace of every Qloo call the agent made.

31
00:01:10,983 --> 00:01:12,599
Already have a city in mind?

32
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:13,710
Type Lisbon.

33
00:01:13,710 --> 00:01:16,162
The agent finds it in Qloo and scores it

34
00:01:16,162 --> 00:01:19,104
for every traveler, with the same taste signals.

35
00:01:19,817 --> 00:01:22,511
Lisbon gets sixty-five, against Qloo's

36
00:01:22,511 --> 00:01:24,639
top pick, Sayulita, at eighty.

37
00:01:24,639 --> 00:01:27,232
Now the group can decide with real numbers.

38
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:31,024
Under the hood, it's the Qloo Insights API.

39
00:01:31,024 --> 00:01:34,149
Search turns each favourite into a Qloo entity.

40
00:01:34,149 --> 00:01:36,726
Destination insights score cities for the whole

41
00:01:36,726 --> 00:01:39,194
group, and filter dot entities re-scores that

42
00:01:39,194 --> 00:01:41,278
exact candidate set for each traveler.

43
00:01:41,278 --> 00:01:45,618
Then place insights, filtered by location, fill the itinerary.

44
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:47,758
TasteMatch Trips.

45
00:01:47,758 --> 00:01:49,737
One trip, everyone's taste.

46
00:01:49,737 --> 00:01:50,994
Try it live, and grab

47
00:01:50,994 --> 00:01:52,850
the open-source code on GitHub.
